• Gideon Sundback redesigned the device in 1913, creating the modern, more reliable zipper.$q$, $q$The student wants to explain why Judson's original design failed to catch on. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["Judson's original 1893 slide fastener frequently jammed, which kept it from becoming commercially successful.","Gideon Sundback redesigned the slide fastener in 1913.","Whitcomb Judson patented an early slide fastener in 1893.","Zippers are now used in countless everyday products."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Only the correct answer gives the specific reason, frequent jamming, that explains why the original design did not catch on.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-198$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
• Peregrine falcons can reach speeds over 240 miles per hour during a diving attack.
• This makes them the fastest animals on Earth in terms of top speed.
• They fold their wings into a streamlined shape to achieve these speeds.$q$, $q$The student wants to emphasize the falcon's status as the fastest animal on Earth. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["Diving at speeds over 240 miles per hour, the peregrine falcon is the fastest animal on Earth.","Peregrine falcons fold their wings into a streamlined shape while diving.","Peregrine falcons are skilled hunters found on every continent except Antarctica.","Many birds of prey rely on speed to catch their prey."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Only the correct answer states the specific speed figure and the falcon's status as fastest animal, directly fulfilling the stated goal.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-199$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 1, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
