  ($q$ei-200$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
• Chameleons change color primarily through specialized cells with pigment and light-reflecting crystals.
• Rather than mainly for camouflage, color change is largely used to signal mood or communicate with other chameleons.
• Temperature also influences a chameleon's coloration.$q$, $q$The student wants to correct the misconception that chameleons change color mainly to hide from predators. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["Although often assumed to change color mainly to hide from predators, chameleons primarily use color shifts to signal mood and communicate with other chameleons.","Chameleons change color using specialized cells containing pigment and light-reflecting crystals.","Temperature can influence a chameleon's coloration.","Many reptiles have evolved ways to blend into their surroundings."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Only the correct answer directly names and corrects the common misconception about camouflage, matching the stated goal.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-201$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
• A blue whale's heart can weigh as much as 400 pounds.
• Its heartbeat can be detected from over a mile away using specialized equipment.
• Blue whales are the largest animals known to have ever lived.$q$, $q$The student wants to use a specific detail to illustrate the enormous size of a blue whale's heart. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["A blue whale's heart can weigh as much as 400 pounds, large enough that its heartbeat can be detected from over a mile away.","Blue whales are the largest animals known to have ever lived.","A blue whale's heartbeat can be detected using specialized equipment.","A blue whale's heart can weigh as much as 400 pounds."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Only the correct answer combines the heart's weight with the mile-away detectable heartbeat to fully illustrate its enormous size; the choices about the heart's weight or its detectable heartbeat each give only one of those two details, and the choice calling blue whales the largest animals describes overall size, not the heart.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-202$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
• The Great Chicago Fire of 1871 destroyed roughly 3.3 square miles of the city.
