• The sound produced can briefly reach louder levels than a gunshot.$q$, $q$The student wants to emphasize how loud the pistol shrimp's claw snap can be. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["A pistol shrimp's claw snap can briefly produce a sound louder than a gunshot.","A pistol shrimp's claw snap creates a shockwave that can stun or kill small prey.","Pistol shrimp use a specialized claw to capture their prey.","Many marine animals rely on sound to communicate or hunt."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Only the correct answer states the specific comparison to a gunshot, directly fulfilling the goal of emphasizing the snap's loudness.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-208$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
• Pierre de Coubertin helped revive the Olympic Games in 1896 after more than 1,500 years of dormancy.
• The first modern Games featured only 14 nations and roughly 241 athletes.
• Women were not permitted to compete until the 1900 Games in Paris.$q$, $q$The student wants to emphasize how small the first modern Olympics were compared to today. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["The first modern Olympics in 1896 drew only about 241 athletes from 14 nations, a tiny fraction of the thousands who compete today.","Pierre de Coubertin helped revive the Olympic Games in 1896.","Women were not permitted to compete in the Olympics until 1900.","The Olympic Games have a long and storied history."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Only the correct answer gives the specific small numbers of athletes and nations, directly fulfilling the goal of emphasizing the first Games' modest scale.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-209$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 1, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
• László Bíró patented a reliable ballpoint pen design in 1938.
