• Within months, X-ray machines were being used in hospitals to examine broken bones.$q$, $q$The student wants to use a specific detail to illustrate how quickly X-rays were put to practical medical use. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["Just months after Röntgen's 1895 discovery, hospitals were already using X-ray machines to examine patients' broken bones.","Röntgen discovered X-rays while experimenting with cathode ray tubes.","One of Röntgen's first X-ray images showed his wife's hand and wedding ring.","Medical imaging technology has continued to advance since the 1890s."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Only the correct answer gives the specific timeframe, within months, showing how quickly X-rays reached practical hospital use.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-216$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
• Factory A automated its assembly line in 2015; worker injury rates fell by 45% by 2021.
• Factory B delayed automation until 2020; worker injury rates fell by only 10% over the same period.
• Both factories produce similar goods and employ similarly sized workforces.$q$, $q$The student wants to use the data to suggest that earlier automation, rather than workforce differences, explains Factory A's greater drop in injuries. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["Although Factory A and Factory B employ similarly sized workforces, Factory A's earlier automation was followed by a 45% drop in injuries by 2021, compared to only a 10% drop at Factory B.","Factory A automated its assembly line in 2015.","Factory B delayed automating its assembly line until 2020.","Factory A and Factory B produce similar goods."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Only the correct answer combines the comparable-workforce detail with both factories' injury-rate changes to suggest automation timing, not workforce size, drove the gap.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-217$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
