  ($q$ei-450$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Coral reefs cover less than 1% of the ocean floor.
• They support about 25% of marine species.
• Rising ocean temperatures cause coral bleaching.$q$, $q$The student wants to argue that protecting reefs is disproportionately valuable. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["Although coral reefs cover less than 1% of the ocean floor, they support about 25% of marine species, so protecting them benefits a vast share of ocean life.","About 25% of marine species live in the ocean.","Coral reefs cover very little of the ocean floor.","Rising ocean temperatures cause coral bleaching."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The correct choice contrasts the reefs' small area with their outsized role.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-451$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Sojourner Truth was born into slavery in New York around 1797.
• She escaped in 1826.
• In 1851 she delivered a famous speech on women's rights in Akron, Ohio.$q$, $q$The student wants to trace her path from slavery to public advocacy. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["Born into slavery around 1797, Sojourner Truth escaped in 1826 and later became a leading speaker for women's rights.","Sojourner Truth was born in New York.","Sojourner Truth gave a speech in Akron.","Sojourner Truth escaped in 1826 and gave speeches."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The correct choice covers the progression from slavery through escape to advocacy.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-452$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Wind turbines generate no emissions during operation.
• Manufacturing turbines requires energy and materials.
• A turbine typically offsets the emissions from its manufacture within a year.$q$, $q$The student wants to acknowledge a drawback of wind turbines while emphasizing their environmental benefit. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["Wind turbines generate no emissions.","Manufacturing turbines requires energy and materials.","A turbine can offset emissions.","Although manufacturing a wind turbine requires energy and materials, a typical turbine offsets those emissions within a year and then operates without emissions."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The correct choice includes both the drawback and the offsetting benefit.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-453$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• The Library of Congress holds more than 170 million items.
• It was established in 1800.
• It is the largest library in the world by collection size.$q$, $q$The student wants to emphasize the size of the Library of Congress. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["The Library of Congress was established in 1800.","Libraries hold books and other items.","The Library of Congress is in the United States.","The Library of Congress, which holds more than 170 million items, is the largest library in the world by collection size."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Only the correct choice emphasizes its size.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-454$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 1, $q$While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Octopuses have eight arms.
• They can change color to match their surroundings.
